<title>GERMANY: Deutsche declines comment on Axiom bid report.</title>
<headline>Deutsche declines comment on Axiom bid report.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Deutsche Bank AG on Monday declined comment on a British press report that its MGAM London fund management arm was in the bidding for Australian fund manager Axiom.</p>
<p>The Observer newspaper reported on Sunday that Morgan Grenfell Asset Management was one of four shortlisted bidders for Axiom along with National Australia Bank, Macquarie Bank, and Dutch group Mercantile Mutual.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no comment,&quot; a Deutsche spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Observer said National Australia was the favoured bidder for Axiom which manages funds worth A$18 billion for the New South Wales government.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
